            "description": "Watch Mansfield Town vs Cardiff highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 2, 2026. On May 2, 2026, Mansfield Town hosted Cardiff in a League One clash that quickly developed into a breathless display of attacking football. The atmosphere at the stadium was charged from the outset, setting the stage for an afternoon defined by constant shifts in momentum and clinical finishing in front of goal. A Blistering Start for the Hosts The home side signaled their intent immediately, with Ryan Sweeney putting Mansfield Town in front just two minutes into the match, following an assist from Nathan Moriah-Welsh . The rapid tempo continued as Lucas Akins doubled the lead in the 23rd minute, set up by Louis Reed . Before the visitors could find their rhythm, Akins struck again just three minutes later, finishing off a ball from Will Evans to establish a commanding early advantage. The first half remained a tactical test for Cardiff , as they struggled to contain the clinical efficiency of the Mansfield frontline, eventually heading into the break facing a significant mountain to climb. The Second Half Resurgence The second period began with a tactical shake-up as both sides sought to control the match . Cardiff found a foothold in the 61st minute when Isaak Davies converted an assist from Ollie Tanner , cutting into the deficit. However, Mansfield responded instantly; Rhys Oates restored the three-goal cushion just two minutes later, thanks to another assist from Louis Reed . As the second half progressed, the game transformed into an end-to-end spectacle. Omari Kellyman , having entered the fray earlier, found the back of the net for Cardiff in the 67th minute, assisted by Rubin Colwill . The tension rose further when Oliver Irow netted Mansfield ’s fifth goal in the 79th minute, once again teed up by Louis Reed . Despite the scoreline, Cardiff refused to fade away, with Ronan Kpakio scoring in the 86th minute to bring the visitors within two. A final surge from Cardiff saw Omari Kellyman grab his second of the game in stoppage time, but the clock ultimately favored the hosts, who held on to secure a dramatic result in a truly memorable sports occasion."
